  "solution": "**Given:**\n\ndfrac{(0.85)³ - (0.1)³}{(0.85)² + 0.085 + 0.01} = ?\n\n**Formula used:**\n\na³ - b³ = (a - b)(a² + ab + b²)\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n⇒ dfrac{(0.85 - 0.1)(0.85² + 0.85 times 0.1 + 0.1²)}{0.85² + 0.085 + 0.01}\n\n⇒ dfrac{(0.75)(0.85² + 0.085 + 0.01)}{0.85² + 0.085 + 0.01}\n\n⇒ 0.75\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**",
